From d6fe4872a02d988e950605aa95ed5d9725ea6da2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saalim Quadri <danascape@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:40:10 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] rust: allow Clang-native RANDSTRUCT configs

*** Do not apply. Recorded with the measurement showing it does not work.

CONFIG_RUST has carried "depends on !RANDSTRUCT" since 2f7ab1267dc9
("Kbuild: add Rust support"), which predates Clang's randstruct. Clang
reorders the FieldDecl chain, which libclang reports, so the dependency
looks stale. It is not.

bindgen emits an anonymous struct or union member of a randomized record
first, at offset 0, rather than where Clang put it:

  struct t {
          long m0;
          union { int u0; long u1; };
          long m2;
          long m3;
  } __randomize_layout;

  Clang    m3 @0  m2 @8  union @16  m0 @24
  bindgen  union @0  m3 @8  m2 @16  m0 @24

With randstruct off it is placed correctly. Reproduced with bindgen 0.72.1
and 0.73.2 against clang 22.0.1 and 22.0.2.

Comparing clang -fdump-record-layouts against rustc's layout of the emitted
bindings over rust/bindings/bindings_helper.h, 5350 member offsets with
randstruct off disagree nowhere; with it on, 235 of 5351 disagree, in cred,
file, inode, mm_struct, shmem_inode_info, task_struct and vm_area_struct.
Over ten seeds the off arm is 0 every time and the on arm ranges 134 to 413.

An x86_64 emulator kernel with this and CONFIG_RANDSTRUCT_FULL=y does not
finish booting. ashmem_vmfile_get_unmapped_area() reads current->mm, which
sits at 376 while Rust reads 384 -- migration_node -- and passes it to
mm_get_unmapped_area(). mmap returns EINVAL and system_server dies in a loop:

  E Zygote: java.lang.RuntimeException: Failed to mmap shared memory: Invalid argument
  E Zygote:   at com.android.internal.os.ApplicationSharedMemory.nativeMap(Native Method)

pid and tgid agreed on that kernel, so a spot check of a few members passes.
vermagic does not catch it either: the hash covers the seed, which both sides
agreed on.

Gating on CC_IS_CLANG is still the right shape, but not until bindgen places
anonymous members at their randomized offsets and the build checks it did.

Link: https://lkml.iu.edu/2411.2/03251.html
Signed-off-by: Saalim Quadri <danascape@gmail.com>
---
 init/Kconfig | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/init/Kconfig b/init/Kconfig
index 602f9b330b76..01e479ac5999 100644
--- a/init/Kconfig
+++ b/init/Kconfig
@@ -2129,8 +2129,7 @@ config RUST
 	depends on RUST_IS_AVAILABLE
 	select EXTENDED_MODVERSIONS if MODVERSIONS
 	depends on !MODVERSIONS || GENDWARFKSYMS
-	depends on !GCC_PLUGIN_RANDSTRUCT
-	depends on !RANDSTRUCT
+	depends on !RANDSTRUCT || CC_IS_CLANG
 	depends on !DEBUG_INFO_BTF || (PAHOLE_HAS_LANG_EXCLUDE && !LTO)
 	depends on !CFI || HAVE_CFI_ICALL_NORMALIZE_INTEGERS_RUSTC
 	select CFI_ICALL_NORMALIZE_INTEGERS if CFI
